    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0009006 -->

    <Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0009006">
        <rdfs:label>shoot system</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0025007"/>
        <disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0025025"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>thallus (related)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Poaceae crown (related)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FNA:02756ad4-a09c-48d7-8754-903254e557a9</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>sistema de epiblasto (epiblastema) (Spanish, exact)</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>thalli (related, plural)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>plant_anatomy</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <ns4:IAO_0000115>A collective plant organ structure (PO:0025007) that produces shoot-borne portions of meristem tissue (PO:0009013) and the plant structures (PO:0009011) that arise from them.</ns4:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>The shoot system is generally used to refer to the above-ground plant parts, although some plants have parts of their shoot system underground. For example, a rhizome (PO:0004542), bulb (PO:0025356), a corm (PO:0025355) or a subterranean tuber (PO:0004547), as in Solanum tuberosum (potato) or yam, are all part of the shoot system.</rdfs:comment>
        <oboInOwl:id>PO:0009006</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PO_GIT:135</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>shoot (related)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>シュート系、苗条系 (Japanese, exact)</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>tree crown (narrow)</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FNA:d1431b5c-7b86-46a0-8d3c-bd426fe12c85</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
